---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy | LicensingMadeSimple" description="What LicensingMadeSimple collects, the tools it uses, and how to ask about your information.">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p>Last updated October 19, 2026</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container article" style="max-width: 720px;">
      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>The roadmap on the home page keeps the choices you click (business type, license type, and state count) in your browser while you use that page. It does not ask for your name, email, or phone, and it does not send those choices to us.</p>
      <p>If you email us, we receive the message you send, including your email address and whatever you write.</p>

      <h2>Tools we use</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>We count page views with Cloudflare Web Analytics. It sets no cookies and does not follow you across sites. It records the page, referrer, browser type and country, in aggregate.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>This site sets no cookies.</p>

      <h2>Your choices and requests</h2>
      <p>To ask what we hold about you, or to have it corrected or deleted, email <a href="mailto:privacy@licensingmadesimple.com">privacy@licensingmadesimple.com</a>.</p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>We may update this policy by posting a new version on this page and changing the date above.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Email <a href="mailto:privacy@licensingmadesimple.com">privacy@licensingmadesimple.com</a>.</p>

      <h2>Chrome extension</h2>
      <p>Privacy practices for the License Expiration Tracker Chrome extension are described separately: <a href="/privacy/chrome-license-expiration-tracker/">Privacy policy for the License Expiration Tracker Chrome extension</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .article h2 { font-size: 1.15rem; margin-top: 32px; margin-bottom: 10px; }
  .article h2:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  .article p { font-size: 0.92rem; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .article ul { font-size: 0.92rem; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.7; margin: 0 0 12px 1.2em; padding: 0; }
  .article li { margin-bottom: 6px; }
</style>
